The infamous focus border issue. I've dealt with this one many times before, and I'm happy to help you out. To remove the border highlight on an input text element in Safari and Chrome, you can use the `outline-remove` property. Simply add the following CSS rule to your stylesheet:
```
input:focus {
  outline-remove: true;
}
```
This will completely remove the focus border, giving you a much cleaner look. Note that you can also use the `outline-remove` property to customize the appearance of the focus border, by setting it to a specific color or style. For example:
```
input:focus {
  outline-remove: dashed #ccc;
}
```
This will replace the default blue border with a dashed gray border.

As for IE, I can tell you that it behaves similarly to Safari and Chrome, in that it will also display a focus border by default. However, you can use the `border-focus` property to control its appearance. Simply set `border-focus` to `none` to remove the border altogether:
```
input:focus {
  border-focus: none;
}
```
This should work in all versions of IE, from 7 onwards. I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.

